comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T23:05:15.992Z",pi-agent,"Test coverage added in test/lineage.test.ts: the approved-budget refusal verified revert-proof (commenting out the refusal makes the assertion fail with 'Missing expected rejection'), countPromotedUnderApproval counting promotions under one approval and skipping unparseable generations, the seed consuming no budget, and a permitted-promotions budget consumed one unit at a time."
  "2026-08-11T09:12:30.362Z","harness:claude-code","Corrective note: an earlier comment on this item describes countPromotedUnderApproval as SKIPPING a generation whose specification cannot be read. That was the behaviour when the comment was written and it is no longer true.\n\nThe shipped behaviour refuses. A generation with no JSON fence, or one whose spec fails to parse, makes the approved budget undecidable and the promotion is refused with budget_undecidable and exit code 4, naming the offending generation id and the reason. Treating unreadable provenance as absent provenance inverts the contract the budget exists to enforce, because the budget bounds a recursive loop that promotes programmatically and cannot notice a silently skipped record.\n\nThe budget guarantee this item delivers also changed twice after the item was first closed, so the current statement of it is: the promoted count and the promotion write are held in ONE workspace writer lock via commitWorkspaceTransaction; concurrent promotions serialize rather than one being refused for contention, so a loser re-reads the count the winner just changed and reports the accurate terminal budget_exceeded; and the already-promoted check is re-run INSIDE that lock, because the pre-lock check reads state every concurrent caller sees before any of them holds the lock, which let three concurrent promotions of one generation all succeed.\n\nRecording this as an appended corrective entry rather than editing the original, so the sequence of what was believed when stays legible."
close_reason: Approved generation budget test coverage complete
